# Research an unclear ask before building it

When the original ask leaves a point unclear, look it up before writing that point. Do not pick an interpretation and ship it.

Read the ask first. For anything it does not settle, read the reference it names: that product's own docs, README, and the format it stores. The plan for the unclear part comes from that reading. Then build.

A screenshot from David is a check after the reading, not a substitute for it. A guess that contradicts the ask is a wrong execution, not a clarification.

Folia and Asana are the kanban reference in the Project board ask. Their docs already separate a column (a status) from a todo (a checkbox on the card) and open the card's fields in a detail panel. Inventing a different shape, then waiting to be corrected, skips this step.
